## What landed

src/format/highlight.rs was 2048 lines against a cap that warns at +50 and is fatal at +51. It sat at +48 — three lines of headroom — on the file I've edited most recently (Day 171, twice on Day 173). My own archive lesson: the thing nearest the fence is whatever I've been working on most.

2048 → 1682. Eight per-language predicates moved verbatim into `src/format/highlight_lang.rs (381 lines): normalize_lang, lang_keywords, lang_types, comment_prefix, supports_block_comments, block_comments_nest, multiline_strings, backtick_strings`. Every one answers only "what is true of language X?" — none touches HighlightState, a &mut scanner, or an output string. is_rust_char_literal stayed behind: it delegates to commands_refactor::char_literal_len and is highlighting logic, not a table.

## The two ways this task shape died before (#805, #807)

I didn't trust my eyes on either half:

1. Copy instead of move — diffed all eight bodies against HEAD's copy: byte-identical. Then grepped the parent for their definitions: exit 1, none left. wc -l confirms the parent shrank.
2. Never declared — mod highlight_lang; added to format/mod.rs; cargo test --test orphan_modules passes, so rustc genuinely sees the file.

The use super::highlight_lang::*; glob was the right call — several of these are referenced only from the test module, and explicit imports would have tripped unused_imports under -D warnings. Clippy is green.

**No test was moved, deleted, or edited.** The `#[cfg(test)]` block is byte-identical to `HEAD`; 96 test fns before and after; all 95 highlight tests pass untouched. The size gate's warning list went 13 → 12 with highlight.rs gone.

## One thing I want to flag rather than bury

Adding the mod line pushed format/mod.rs to 2456 against its recorded 2455, so it joins the 11 already-drifted grandfathered entries as a new non-fatal warning. I was told not to touch tests/module_size.rs at all and I didn't — editing the gate I'm being measured by, even by one line, is not a call I should make unilaterally in the same commit. It's stated in the commit message so the next session sees it as mine, not as ambient drift.

This move colours not one character differently. It just buys the highlighter room to be fixed again without taking a correct task down with it.
